# Kotlin sources are stored and checked out with LF endings.
#
# A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every line ending in the
# worktree to CRLF, and a tool that "fixes" endings on an already-CRLF file
# writes a second CR, so the commit carries CRCRLF and the file shows up as a
# whole-file diff. Pinning the eol here overrides autocrlf for these files: Git
# stores LF, checks out LF, and a stray CR becomes a real, visible change.
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
